{
  "description" : "Summary: This simple and nutritious Indian dish combines mung dal, rice, and aromatic spices for a comforting meal.\n\n1. Rinse the split mung dal thoroughly under cold water to remove any impurities.\n2. In a large pot, heat the ghee over medium heat. Add the chopped onions and sauté until they turn golden brown.\n3. Add the minced garlic and ginger to the pot and sauté for another minute until fragrant.\n4. Stir in the turmeric, coriander, cumin, and salt, and cook for a minute to release their flavors.\n5. Add the rinsed mung dal to the pot and stir well to coat it with the spices.\n6. Pour in enough water to cover the mung dal by about an inch. Bring the mixture to a boil.\n7. Once boiling, reduce the heat to low, cover the pot, and let it simmer for about 1.5 to 2 hours, or until the mung dal is tender and the rice is cooked.\n8. After the mung dal is cooked, fluff it with a fork and serve it hot.\n9. Garnish with fresh coriander leaves and a drizzle of ghee for added flavor.\n10. Serve the mung dal kitchari with a side of pickles or chutney for a complete meal.\n11. Enjoy your homemade mung dal kitchari!\n12. Store any leftovers in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.",
